      "title": "Base Units",
      "language": "en",
      "source_refs": [
        {
          "source_document_id": "e2c5c034-041b-5340-9823-5e3c8c88a07c",
          "pdf_from": 5,
          "pdf_to": 5,
          "note": "Base Units: a main subheading of 1.2 International System of Units, its own page (owner 2026-11-04); PDF 5-5."
        }
      ],
      "body": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "There are seven base units for physical quantities namely: length, mass, time, temperature, electric current, light or luminous intensity and amount of substance (with special reference to the number of particles). Prefixes such as milli, micro, kilo, etc. may be used with them to express smaller or larger quantities."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "The names of base units for these physical quantities together with symbols are listed in Table 1.1."
          },
          {
            "type": "table",
            "caption": "Table 1.1",
            "header": [
              "Physical Quantity",
              "SI Unit",
              "Symbol"
            ],
            "rows": [
              [
                "Length",
                "metre",
                "m"
              ],
              [
                "Mass",
                "kilogram",
                "kg"
              ],
              [
